    "row1": { "x": 0, "y": -260, "text": "1 · Access and coach scheduling", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 5960 },
    "row2": { "x": 0, "y": 960, "text": "2 · Approval flow", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3000 },
    "row3": { "x": 0, "y": 2280, "text": "3 · Super admin setup", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 4000 },
    "legend": { "x": -700, "y": 0, "w": 560, "color": "red", "text": "Brand\n\nCrimson #AD0303, black #0A0A0A, light grey #F5F5F5 — the same set the Jr Chargers tryout and camp materials use. Barlow Condensed for headings and team names, Barlow for body, IBM Plex Mono for times.\n\nHow a block reads on the calendar\n\nReserved — solid crimson, team name in white. Approved and locked.\n\nPending — crimson dashed outline over diagonal stripes. Requested but not decided; the slot is already held, and the requesting team's name is visible.\n\nClosed — grey hatch. Outside that day's hours, or a closure date.\n\nFill vs. outline vs. hatch, so the three read apart in greyscale too.\n\nOne facility, one bookable space." },
    "flow": { "x": -700, "y": 1220, "w": 560, "color": "gray", "text": "The loop\n\nCoach picks an open slot → picks a length (30 / 60 / 90 min) → submits.\n\nThe request lands in the approver's inbox AND in the Approvals queue. Both do the same thing; whoever gets there first decides it.\n\nApprove → the block fills solid crimson with the team name. Decline → approver types a reason, coach sees it in email and in My requests.\n\nApprove is the solid crimson button; Decline is the black outline. Never two reds." }
  }
